<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34371" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pĕdum</span></b> , i, n.,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a town of
				remote antiquity in Latium</i>, <i>near Rome</i>,
			prob. the mod. <i>Gallicano</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 2,
			39</span></i>; <i><span class="en">8, 12</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">13</span></i>.—
			Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pĕdānus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>of
			Pedum</i>, <i>Pedan</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">regio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor. Ep. 1, 4, 2</span></i>
			.—<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pĕdānum</span></b> , i,
				n. (sc. praedium), <i>an estate near
				Pedum</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Att. 9, 18, 3</span></i>.—<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pĕdāni</span></b> ,
				ōrum, m., <i>the inhabitants of Pedum</i>, <i>the Pedans</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Liv. 8,
				14</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
